  "Number": 5,
  "Question": "The area of a circle whose circumference is \\(24\\pi\\) is \\(k\\pi.\\) What is the value of \\(k?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\)",
    "B": "\\(12\\)",
    "C": "\\(24\\)",
    "D": "\\(36\\)",
    "E": "\\(144\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The area formula needs the radius, so first recover it from the circumference. Let \\(r>0\\) be the circle's radius. Using circumference \\(2\\pi r\\),\n\\[\n2\\pi r=24\\pi,\n\\qquad r=12.\n\\]\nThe area is therefore \\(\\pi r^2=\\pi\\cdot12^2=144\\pi\\). Comparing this with \\(k\\pi\\) gives \\(k=\\boxed{144}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
